{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "שש עגלות", :translit "shesh eglot", :gloss "six wagons"} {:he "ששה מזלות", :translit "shishah mazlot", :gloss "six constellations"} {:he "ששה עתים", :translit "shishah itim", :gloss "six seasons"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Symbolic correspondence: six wagons mapped to six ascending and six descending constellations and to six seasonal times."}], :frame {:text "Six constellations ascend and six descend in the celestial sphere, and Genesis 1:14 speaks of the luminaries for signs and for seasons (לאתת ולמועדים), understood as including the seasonal divisions of cold, heat, summer, winter, seedtime, and harvest.", :sources ["Genesis 1:14" "Genesis 8:22"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ושני עשר בקר", :translit "ushnei asar bakar", :gloss "and twelve oxen"} {:he "י\"ב שבטים", :translit "shneim asar shevatim", :gloss "twelve tribes"} {:he "י\"ב מזלות", :translit "shneim asar mazlot", :gloss "twelve constellations"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Symbolic correspondence: twelve oxen mapped to twelve tribes of Israel and twelve zodiac constellations."}], :frame {:text "The twelve tribes of Israel correspond to the twelve zodiac constellations. Each tribe is associated with a constellation in Talmudic and Midrashic sources; the twelve sons of Jacob are enumerated in Genesis 49 as twelve, and the twelve constellations are enumerated in m. Shabbat 7:2.", :sources ["Genesis 49" "m. Shabbat 7:2"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Symbolic correspondence: six wagons mapped to six ascending and six descending constellations and to six seasonal times.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Symbolic correspondence: twelve oxen mapped to twelve tribes of Israel and twelve zodiac constellations.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:27:29.923444645Z", :model "glm-5.2"}